(3501477, 485495, 72200, '<td valign="top">Actually there were three light sources, although I admit it isn''t obvious, which I thought would hurt me. There was natural light coming from a window opposite the couch this was taken on. I also used a directional light from the left rear, adding illuminating her body. The third was a reflective light on the right to fill in some of the detail on the right side of her face. I haven''t done a lot of ''studio'' shots, so it''s still experimental to me. I don''t have any ''professional'' lights, so I just make use of house lamps, foil covered poster board, fabric or whatever I can get to work for now. Thanks for your input.</td>', 'Actually there were three light sources, although I admit it isn''t obvious, which I thought would hurt me. There was natural light coming from a window opposite the couch this was taken on. I also used a directional light from the left rear, adding illuminating her body. The third was a reflective light on the right to fill in some of the detail on the right side of her face. I haven''t done a lot of ''studio'' shots, so it''s still experimental to me. I don''t have any ''professional'' lights, so I just make use of house lamps, foil covered poster board, fabric or whatever I can get to work for now. Thanks for your input.', '2007-03-31 02:47:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3502541, 485153, 52130, '<td valign="top">I think this was a good idea that just lacked something. The lighting is a little too orange, maybe it could have been more blueish? Also, it''s hard to tell what''s in the other hand, is it a knife? maybe just a tad more lighting form another source might have helped this.</td>', 'I think this was a good idea that just lacked something. The lighting is a little too orange, maybe it could have been more blueish? Also, it''s hard to tell what''s in the other hand, is it a knife? maybe just a tad more lighting form another source might have helped this.', '2007-03-31 18:54:08.000000', NULL, 0),
